\section{Interpretive ledger}
For clarity, the audit classifies outcomes rather than ranking them:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \EqClass{Balanced}: the fixed map produces equal or dimensionless coefficients without further discretionary choices (e.g. a \(c\)-wave, vacuum Maxwell with \(\widetilde B=cB\)).
  \item \EqClass{Scaled}: the map exposes a characteristic length, inverse length, or dimensionless ratio (e.g. \(D/c\), \(\nu/c\), \(\hbar/(mc)\), \(GM/c^2\)).
  \item \EqClass{Structured residue}: derivative order, nonlinearity, dispersion, collision structure, signature, or topology persists.
  \item \EqClass{Null action}: the base temporal map does nothing because the law contains no time variable.
\end{itemize}
A useful theory of the audit would explain why these classes recur and whether the list closes under a preregistered expansion of the battery.

